<h1 class="page-title">Practical Stock Planner</h1>
<p class="tagline">Time-phased stock planning for Windows</p>

<section class="card">
  <div class="content">
    <p>Know what to order, and when, before you run out.</p>
    <p>
      Practical Stock Planner is a Windows desktop app for product businesses that buy in stock from suppliers with lead times. It projects your stock period by period from your stock on hand, open purchase orders and forecast. It shows, for each item, where you will run short, and it tells you what to order and when to order it.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is practical, not theoretical. No black box. You can see the inputs, check the maths, and stay in control of every purchasing decision.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Period by period projection.</strong> See projected stock for each item, period by period, based on your forecast, stock on hand and orders already placed. It plans over time, not from a single reorder point.</li>
      <li><strong>Shortage warnings.</strong> Spot the periods where stock will drop below where you want it, before it happens.</li>
      <li><strong>Order suggestions.</strong> Get suggested order quantities and order dates that allow for supplier lead times.</li>
      <li><strong>Open purchase orders included.</strong> Stock you have already ordered is counted in the period it is due to arrive.</li>
      <li><strong>Imports from CSV files.</strong> Save them from Excel or Google Sheets, filling in the app&rsquo;s templates from the exports your current systems already produce. There is no direct connection to those systems.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it&rsquo;s for</h2>
    <p>
      Product businesses that buy in stock from suppliers with lead times (online stores, wholesalers, distributors and brands) and have outgrown spreadsheet reorder lists or simple reorder points.
    </p>

    <h2>What it doesn&rsquo;t do</h2>
    <p>We want you to know before you buy:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>It plans <strong>one stock location</strong>. It does not plan multiple warehouses or stores.</li>
      <li>It is <strong>not manufacturing planning</strong>. There is no bill of materials (recipes or components) and no production scheduling.</li>
      <li>It does not place orders with your suppliers or change anything in your other systems. It gives you a plan; you decide.</li>
      <li>It runs on <strong>Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit</strong> only.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your data stays on your PC</h2>
    <p>
      Your stock, sales, forecast and supplier data stay on your own PC. We never see them. The app only contacts our licence server to check your licence.
    </p>
    <p>
      The exception is Guided setup. If you choose it, you send me CSV files so I can check them for your setup. I use those files only for your setup. They are kept private and deleted within 30 days of the call. Day to day, the app still does not send your planning data. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

